The escape character detection is incomplete. A string like `'test\\\\'quote'` would incorrectly detect the quote as unescaped because `prevChar` would be a backslash, but that backslash itself is escaped. Consider implementing proper escape sequence handling that tracks whether the backslash itself is escaped.
```suggestion

      // Track string literals (simple handling of " and ')
      if (char === '"' || char === "'") {
        // Determine if this quote character is escaped by counting
        // the number of consecutive backslashes immediately before it.
        let backslashCount = 0;
        for (let j = i - 1; j >= 0 && content[j] === '\\'; j--) {
          backslashCount++;
        }
        const isEscaped = backslashCount % 2 === 1;

        if (!isEscaped) {
          if (!inString) {
            inString = true;
            stringChar = char;
          } else if (char === stringChar) {
            inString = false;
            stringChar = '';
          }
        }
```
